{"title":"2006 IMO Shortlist Problems/G2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Ukraine</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1788ec6ad85848dbaeacf2cea3bf65bc2fef76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle ABCD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> be a trapezoid with parallel sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a41873f25c9730b549a20443c89f11ff563211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} \\displaystyle AB &gt;CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />.  Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c31f3404a91311bb4be7cec9d49bb510d592d34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle K$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1e3168ff93ce6ae8adc13c43870dcee9c0b2e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle L$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> lie on the line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/5931cc41be74baf9c04dd152b800fe8a9fcda24c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle AB$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee17cb25d501dce5acb115a17941e36127df93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle CD$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, respectively, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410deb540911559c8e1af94a4518923759361687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} \\displaystyle AK/KB = DL/LC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />.  Suppose that there are points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec491f5a13233236733b485a8534dbcf6b01ea7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle P$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8eb04937fb64e00e48ea872a5cb960a791fcb3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> on the line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7af1d39653141b0928d7afec2d160f38dc896b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> satisfying\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73212780e957539c37477a63943ecdda3816187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB = \\angle BCD$\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2845438deae48bda79d4d6d85501ebe7237ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CQD = \\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Prove that the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec491f5a13233236733b485a8534dbcf6b01ea7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle P$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8eb04937fb64e00e48ea872a5cb960a791fcb3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/69551f79ad7ed538f1ba40113c40a5a8573e1d2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} \\displaystyle C$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> are concyclic.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/648f9aa7cabeaf156bfeda343998128aec86b683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} \\displaystyle A,B,K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2eef6b17a21efd269dc55aba3afa80de318ee133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle D,C,L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear, the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410deb540911559c8e1af94a4518923759361687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} \\displaystyle AK/KB = DL/LC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> is equivalent to the condition that lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d800a31db5b1ee845dabe491337e617021a205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle AD$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7af1d39653141b0928d7afec2d160f38dc896b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999a25b627b5ddfe0a6af29e0d4b635adc2cc483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle BC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> are concurrent.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47736949a2a26fa60c778fc69b1a281d43b3a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle X$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> be the point of concurrence.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1c066d278549f312f1907615ee7ab65422522f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\omega_1, \\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> be the circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c631684f3e436df155f0b9d9f8b035582140f43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle APB, DQC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />, respectively.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/720867929ade45bf13927b6567a6b19720fa7657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XBA = \\angle BCD = \\angle APB$\" width=\"218\" height=\"13\" />, the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8310cf088a8ae0f9abd313f982ad527a2bc010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle XB$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08112573154d3f21ac6685fb846812b6b51cb33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />.  Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c9124b946a59cc43bcc98731bd0892ab11476f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8310cf088a8ae0f9abd313f982ad527a2bc010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle XB$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/69551f79ad7ed538f1ba40113c40a5a8573e1d2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} \\displaystyle C$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />.  It follows there is a dilation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/80916f1ea9a71a2fbc9b3e960163b504c931febf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47736949a2a26fa60c778fc69b1a281d43b3a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle X$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> which takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c9124b946a59cc43bcc98731bd0892ab11476f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\omega_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08112573154d3f21ac6685fb846812b6b51cb33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/1/d71cd817e0df9e2f5c854ea9ed6bbbb369717118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle Q&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> denote the image of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8eb04937fb64e00e48ea872a5cb960a791fcb3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/80916f1ea9a71a2fbc9b3e960163b504c931febf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />.  Evidently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd9e6d4c7bc6c1d593b9ec5ab54b6a027fdcdcd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle A, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> are the respective images of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b1a19f0c796aed7e9f17310d51ddb9352c7eff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} \\displaystyle D,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/80916f1ea9a71a2fbc9b3e960163b504c931febf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>Now, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8310cf088a8ae0f9abd313f982ad527a2bc010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle XB$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08112573154d3f21ac6685fb846812b6b51cb33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\omega_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133465fc3d126a47593d2ffc76426cb2e5e9437d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle B$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, it follows that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfdf029a1fb67b5ca158d02bd700c969de1295b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XQ&#39;B = \\angle PQ&#39;B = \\angle XBP = \\angle CBP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"310\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/5691b9b6975b4d1c3a74765dec5e1db64a45497f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle Q&#39;B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> is the image of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/063d26329aeb4e1f6738d4b05cbf0aa08dd5d750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} \\displaystyle QC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> under the dilation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/80916f1ea9a71a2fbc9b3e960163b504c931febf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />, so these two lines are parallel.  Hence\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f86899877927bb014a6c9ced4064b933d6c40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PQC = \\pi - \\angle XQC = \\pi - \\angle XQ&#39;B = \\pi - \\angle CBP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"405\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0de28cac6d3533b652ee47d2418f5c0bb8797ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle P, Q, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> are concyclic, as desired.  <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Halmos&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Halmos (page does not exist)\">Template:Halmos</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/G2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2006 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2006 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/viewtopic.php?p=875014#875014\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018052506\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 273/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 373/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9121/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.438      1 -total\n 65.73%    5.546      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 29.96%    2.528      1 Template:Halmos\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5152:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018052506 and revision id 15781. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}